      "tag": "Gram+ Cocci",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "topic": "S. aureus: scalded skin vs TEN",
      "stem": "A 2-week-old neonate has fever, irritability, and diffuse tender erythema that sloughs with light rubbing (positive Nikolsky sign). The oral mucosa is normal. A skin biopsy would most likely show which finding?",
