      "stem": "A 4-year-old boy has had recurrent liver abscesses and S. aureus lymphadenitis, and one episode of Aspergillus pneumonia. Streptococcal infections have not been a problem. His neutrophils fail to reduce nitroblue tetrazolium. Why are catalase-positive organisms particularly dangerous in this patient?",
