      "explanation": "Dengue (flavivirus, carried by Aedes aegypti mosquitoes) has 4 serotypes. A second infection with a different serotype carries a higher risk of severe dengue (hemorrhage, plasma leakage, shock). Cross-reactive, non-neutralizing IgG binds the virus and helps it enter monocytes through Fc receptors (antibody-dependent enhancement). Treatment is supportive. Avoid NSAIDs and aspirin. The vaccine is used only in people with documented prior infection.",
