      "answer": "D",
      "explanation": "Oral polio vaccine replicates in the gut and induces mucosal IgA, which blocks intestinal replication and interrupts community transmission, so it is preferred for outbreak control. Its drawback is rare reversion to vaccine-associated paralytic polio and circulating vaccine-derived poliovirus. Inactivated vaccine gives excellent systemic protection against paralysis but weaker mucosal immunity, and it cannot revert.",
